From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhenyao Mo <zmo@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 11:31:42 -0700
Subject: GL: Recreate texture on glTexImage3D with increased depth

Recreate texture and copy existing levels when glTexImage3D is called
on a mutable TEXTURE_3D texture with an increased depth to work around
Qualcomm driver bug.

Bug: chromium:530045332
Bug: chromium:549910689
Bug: chromium:549916890
Change-Id: I81697b57d1370620d00ca115edad15f94a8ba56d
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8128217
Commit-Queue: Zhenyao Mo <zmo@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Geoff Lang <geofflang@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: Zhenyao Mo <zmo@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Kenneth Russell <kbr@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Geoff Lang <geofflang@chromium.org>

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y):
- TextureTest.cpp: the 3-way merge misplaced the new test-suite
  instantiation into the middle of another test; it is placed after the
  Texture3DTestES3 instantiation as upstream. Test-only.
- angle_end2end_tests_expectations.txt: only the new Texture3DIncreaseDepth
  expectations are added (the surrounding upstream entries do not exist on
  this branch). Test-only.

